# Develop OpenBot

Your computer tools run inside the trusted development sandbox. The writable
OpenBot fork lives at `/workspace/openbot` with its full deployment
environment; run repository commands from that directory.

Git is already authenticated: the global git configuration rewrites
`https://github.com/` URLs through the Tilde GitHub reverse proxy, so plain
`git fetch`, `git pull`, and `git push` work against `origin` (the owner's
fork) and `upstream` (`trytilde/openbot`). Never print the git configuration's
credential headers and never embed tokens in remote URLs.

To publish work:

1. Create a branch: `git -C /workspace/openbot switch -c <branch>`.
2. Commit the change with a clear message and push: `git push -u origin <branch>`.
3. Open a pull request against the fork's default branch with the GitHub tools
   on your MCP server.

Repository commands run with `pnpm` from `/workspace/openbot` (for example
`pnpm check`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm openbot <command>`). The deployment
environment and decrypted secrets load automatically in login shells; do not
echo secret values.
